WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.210
If your prep is MiraLAX, this video will walk you through exactly how to take

2
00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:04.500
it.

3
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:06.600
Just follow along step by step.

4
00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:10.720
For this prep, you'll need a few items, all available over the counter, no

5
00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:12.000
prescription needed.

6
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:17.610
You'll need one 238-gram bottle of MiraLAX powder, two to four Dulcolax lax

7
00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:18.500
ative tablets,

8
00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:23.500
and 64 ounces of a clear sports drink like Gatorade, Propel, or Crystal Light.

9
00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:26.000
That's usually two 32-ounce bottles.

10
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.800
If you have diabetes, use sugar-free Gatorade G2.

11
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:33.800
Also, make sure you get the laxative tablets, not the stool softener.

12
00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:39.300
One important rule, your sports drink cannot be red, orange, blue, or purple.

13
00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:42.300
Stick to clear or light-colored flavors.

14
00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:46.300
The day before your colonoscopy, you'll start by mixing the solution.

15
00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:50.350
Pour the entire bottle of MiraLAX into a pitcher with all 64 ounces of the

16
00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:51.300
sports drink.

17
00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:54.300
Stir or shake until the powder is completely dissolved.

18
00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:56.800
You can chill it in the refrigerator if you'd like.

19
00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:58.800
Keeping it cold makes it easier to drink.

20
00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:02.300
Now for part one, the evening before your procedure.

21
00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:05.800
At four p.m., take your Dulcolax tablets with a glass of water.

22
00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:08.800
Your doctor's instructions will tell you whether to take two or four.

23
00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:11.300
Follow their guidance on the specific amount.

24
00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:14.300
At five p.m., you'll start drinking the first half of the solution.

25
00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:15.800
That's 32 ounces.

26
00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:19.800
Drink an eight ounce glass every 15 minutes until that half is gone.

27
00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:21.800
Keep drinking clear liquids after you finish.

28
00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:26.890
For part two, six hours before your colonoscopy, you'll drink the second half,

29
00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:28.300
which is another 32 ounces.

30
00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:32.800
Drink this at the same pace, an eight ounce glass every 15 minutes.

31
00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:37.730
You can continue to have clear liquids up until four hours before your

32
00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:38.800
procedure.

33
00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:40.800
This part is really important.

34
00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:44.770
You must drink all of the prep solution as directed even if you're already

35
00:01:44.770 --> 00:01:45.800
passing clear liquid.

36
00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:49.800
I know it can feel like enough, but finishing the entire dose is what gives us

37
00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:51.800
the clearest view during your procedure.

38
00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:55.890
If the prep isn't completed as directed, we may need to reschedule and neither

39
00:01:55.890 --> 00:01:56.800
of us wants that.

40
00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:00.800
Please drink plenty of liquids throughout the process to prevent dehydration.

41
00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:04.800
Staying hydrated will help you feel better and help the prep do its job.

42
00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:08.800
If you experience any discomfort from frequent trips to the bathroom,

43
00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:12.800
applying a petroleum-based ointment or diaper rash cream can really help.

44
00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:14.800
That's it. You've got this.

45
00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:18.800
Follow the timing, finish the full dose, and stay hydrated.

46
00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:21.800
If you have any questions at all, don't hesitate to call our office.

47
00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:22.800
We're here to help.
